    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="1006" n="878" xml:id="pg878"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 674.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cox to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 3, 1885</date>.
                        (Received November 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 44.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 31, dated October 15, is
                    at hand, and in answer thereto I have the honor to state that no further
                    information has reached this legation in reference to the expulsion of the
                    Lubrowsky brothers from Palestine, on account of their religious belief.</p>
                <p>Owing to the prompt action of Mr. Heap, which you commend, I trust that this
                    particular case is concluded, and hope that no more cases of the kind may call
                    for our action.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. S. COX.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
